WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.190
Huh?  There's a food stand here?

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.660
Welcome.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.120
Coffee and two chili dogs please.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.430
Certainly.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.430
Since you have a food stand here...

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.900
...does it mean you’re a 
fan of charisma duelists?

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.930
Of course.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.140
Playmaker is the talk of the day.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.140
Playmaker…

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.100
The mysterious duelist 
who suddenly showed up.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.120
He's charming.  He even saved LINK VRAINS.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.810
Who are you a fan of?

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.370
Playmaker also, I think.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.520
I want to battle him someday.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.250
Here you go.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.730
Are you a duelist too?

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.880
Yeah.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.460
I’ll come again if it’s delicious.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.820
Someone like her goes to LINK VRAINS?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.470
You can’t judge a book by its cover.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.320
Not enough sleep?

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:02.680
Yeah.  I’m busy patrolling 
the net every night.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.620
People upload footage of Playmaker, 
so I have to erase them.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.250
It has to be done consistently.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.160
I see.  In that case, I’ll help.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.700
I run Across the universe

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.870
At the speed of light

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.740
Begin Loading

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.470
Open the door of dreams

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.040
VRAINS spreads

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.150
Believe in myself

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.680
VRAINS continues

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.990
The circuit draws the future

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.060
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.660
Access!

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.360
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:06.970
I'm now With the Wind

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.270
Link with my soul

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.040
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.770
Now Win the Race

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.610
Connected world

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:20.110
No matter when

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.480
Nothing is impossible

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.620
Strive for hope

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.190
And ride the wind!

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.180
Where’s Ai?

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.300
He was being annoying, so I left him at home.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.450
Because I need to think.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.690
About Revolver's speech 
regarding AI with free will?

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:01.880
Yeah.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:06.360
Vanish, Cyberse!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.780
If those are Ai’s memories, 
Revolver destroyed Ai’s world.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.750
#1: Ai’s existence.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.890
#2: Data Storm.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.400
#3: Knights of Hanoi.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.190
These three must be related.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.600
If I can get to Revolver, 
will I learn everything?

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:39.820
Including what happened to me and 
Kusanagi’s brother in the past?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:47.110
I thoroughly reanalyzed Ai’s program, 
but I didn’t learn anything.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.080
I don’t know if he has free will or not.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.430
I’m more concerned about 
what’ll happen next.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:59.290
If an AI gets free will, what will happen?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.250
Hey.  You're overthinking it.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.050
I hope so.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:11.460
If Ai has free will, he's probably 
sad because he's home alone.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.360
You’re ripped!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.430
You’re so cool!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:26.810
Since they’re dumb, they 
don’t know how cool I am.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.240
Dumb is a forbidden word.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.530
Forget that.  Let's do what we always do.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.790
What?  We’re going to do that?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.790
I'm almost complete.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.110
When I'm complete, I’ll 
make you a bit smarter.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.600
Really?

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.740
Gulp.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.450
Is she really coming?

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:58.130
I’m nervous.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.650
Yeah.  It’s like a meetup between gangs.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.920
I’m more charming than a gang.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.260
She’s here, Yamamoto!

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.790
Don’t call me by my real name!

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:15.310
The cyber treasure hunter that 
travels throughout the network!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.860
Ghost Girl!

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:21.320
D-Did you bring what you promised?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.840
Of course.  This is one portion.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.080
Go ahead and inspect it.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.940
It's the Knight of Hanoi and Playmaker!

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:37.220
It’s valuable duel footage of Playmaker vs 
Revolver, the Knights of Hanoi’s leader.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.170
Revolver!

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.690
He’s a villain, but he’s cool!

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.420
After I confirm payment, I’ll 
hand over all the data.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.570
O-Okay!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.570
I just sent the money.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.990
Confirmed.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.980
This is all the data.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:59.770
It includes my interview where 
I answer your questions.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.640
Thank you!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:07.100
Yamamoto and pigeon, maybe 
we’ll meet again someday.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.550
All right!  Let’s get to work!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.420
What is this place?

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.550
It’s an editing room, just for us.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:18.420
Wow!

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:23.190
I negotiated with a higher-up at the 
network to build this within LINK VRAINS.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:27.280
Because it’s quicker to 
edit and transmit from here.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.770
I see!

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.740
We can make a Playmaker TV special!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.330
Ghost Girl's fee was expensive, right?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:43.220
Yeah.  I didn’t have enough money in 
the budget, so I used our future bonuses.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.080
I see.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.400
What?  Mine too?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.650
But if we sell this program, 
we'll get big promotions.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.020
You’re right.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.160
Here's the title of the special!

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.770
Exclusive scoop!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.940
Finally confirmed!

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.490
What's Playmaker’s true identity?

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.170
Ghost Girl reveals the truth about Playmaker!

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.800
You must watch this LINK VRAINS special!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:17.180
We've had Playmaker sightings before, but 
he definitely shows up when Hanoi attacks.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.020
Where’s Ignis?

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.190
I'll crush anyone who gets in my way!

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.170
Vanish!

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.830
Who are you?

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.930
My name is Playmaker!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:38.910
Fine.  You’ll learn what happens 
when you oppose the Hanoi!

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.000
This isn’t good.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.710
His dragon is strong.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.010
You can't win with your current deck.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:46.800
Oh really?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.480
If I lose, you’ll fall 
into Hanoi’s hands.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.450
You should pray that I win.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.890
AIs don’t pray.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.430
We only calculate how to win!

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:05.680
Release Cyberse's data material!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:22.410
This wind…  This is a Speed Duel?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.650
Let’s go!

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.240
Speed Duel!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.130
Appear, Cracking Dragon!

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:49.410
The Data Storm will swallow 
you.  You're terminated.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:58.120
Never-before-seen monsters 
live inside this Data Storm.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.250
Never-before-seen monsters?

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:03.920
Now's the time to use 
your Skill, Storm Access!

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.930
There's no other way for us to survive!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.620
When you have 1000 or fewer LP...

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:16.640
...Storm Access lets you access 
one random card in the Data Storm!

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.580
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:28.960
Now!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.050
Storm Access!

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.360
Link Summon!

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.330
Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.070
Go, Decode Talker!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.540
Decode End!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.420
You have no right to call yourself a duelist!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.900
Playmaker is cool!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.870
Hey, it’s Ghost Girl’s interview.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.870
<i>Witnessed Playmaker
Gorgeous Duelist  Ghost Girl</i>

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:26.530
<i>What's Playmaker's true identity?</i>

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.280
Playmaker’s identity?

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.880
Sorry, but even I don’t know.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:38.780
Not all mysteries can be solved by my beauty.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.540
<i>Why is Playmaker fighting 
the Knights of Hanoi?</i>

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:47.070
He mentioned something about 
an incident ten years ago.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.720
<i>Incident ten years ago?</i>

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:50.560
I’m currently investigating.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.010
<i>Why is SOL Technologies pursuing Playmaker?</i>

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.370
That’s a good question.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:02.010
Because Playmaker acquired an AI 
that affects LINK VRAINS's future.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:05.010
I have what you’re looking for.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.670
Stop attacking LINK VRAINS.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:11.820
If you don’t, I’ll erase it right now!

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.510
Hey hey hey!

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.320
Don't treat your savior as a hostage!

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.820
I see!

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.290
It's starting to feel 
like an exclusive scoop!

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:26.800
After seeing Playmaker, the charisma 
duelists didn’t stay quiet.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:33.950
SOL Technologies hired Go 
Onizuka to battle Playmaker.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:36.730
I’m Go Onizuka.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:42.390
The real hero has arrived 
to unmask the fake hero!

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.030
Link Summon!

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:49.130
Appear, Link 3 Gouki The Great Ogre!

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:51.600
Go, Decode Talker!

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.560
Decode End!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.300
Great Ogre!

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.620
Ogre Axe!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.880
The second assassin was Blue Angel.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.490
Link Summon!

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:25.490
Appear, Link 2 Trickstar Holly Angel!

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:30.600
But Blue Angel was acting strange.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.870
Encode Talker attacks Holly Angel!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.840
Final Encode!

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.180
Everyone doesn't know this, but…

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:53.380
Blue Angel was infected by the 
Knights of Hanoi's computer virus.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.320
Your passion towards Playmaker…

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.170
...has deeply impressed me.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:12.330
I just want you to defeat Playmaker.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:19.690
Due to a misunderstanding, SOL 
Technologies captured Playmaker.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.630
What?

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.530
Really?

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:27.520
What?

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.760
I can’t move!

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:35.140
Playmaker is captured!

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:43.010
That’s when the Knights of 
Hanoi's leader Revolver arrived.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:47.850
He also wanted Playmaker’s AI.

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:50.570
And his power was overwhelming.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.560
Revolver!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.000
Revolver?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.390
A Knight of Hanoi!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:03.660
Let Playmaker go.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:04.360
What?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.690
I’ll be the one to face him.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:13.370
We put a computer virus into 
your sister, Blue Angel.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.280
What?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:22.210
If Playmaker defeats me in a duel, 
I'll give you the removal program.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.640
Playmaker.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:28.460
What I did to you was horrible.

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.260
But for my sister, you'll still...

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.490
You’ll still fight for me 
even though you should hate me?

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:38.490
I don’t hate you.

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:45.420
I only hate the Knights of Hanoi.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:50.070
Here we go!  The hellish duel now begins!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:55.180
I can hear the pulse of the unknown 
power hiding in the network.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:59.610
You’re waiting for me to capture you.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.750
Come, Data Storm!

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.860
I activate my Skill!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.030
The new breath resides in my hand!

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.420
Storm Access!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.430
This power is good.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.960
Link Summon!

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:29.410
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.040
This is bad.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:35.780
There’s only one way we can win.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.120
Storm Access.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:42.590
Sorry, but I won’t let you use that card.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.520
Full Overlap!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:58.600
A Speed Duel is too limiting for our fight.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.840
The next stage is waiting for us.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:05.090
W-What's going on?

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:13.090
The storm swallowed them!

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:14.910
What happened to them?

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.820
Let’s skip further ahead!

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.370
<i>Witnessed Playmaker and Revolver's Duel
Ghost Girl</i>

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:22.000
I gave up trying to enter the storm.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.800
But then a miracle occurred.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:28.270
Maybe God smiled upon my beauty.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.100
I risked my life and successfully entered.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:37.140
The duel for LINK VRAINS's 
future had already started.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:41.610
Playmaker was in a dangerous state.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:46.280
It seems you don’t know what Ignis is.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:49.290
I’ll tell you before you lose.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:52.000
Ignis isn’t a regular AI.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:56.890
Ignis is AI with free will.

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.170
Free will?

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.770
No way!  A program can't have free will!

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:08.790
I naturally expected that reaction.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:15.250
But it doesn’t matter if you 
believe this story or not.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:20.950
Now I'll continue this duel and end you!

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:23.260
Here I go, Playmaker!

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:26.590
My new wind that pierces 
through the closed world!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.010
Link Summon!

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:32.280
Appear, Link 4 Borreload Dragon!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.730
It's his ace monster!

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:50.880
Due to Fire Prison’s effect, your 
Cyberse monsters have vanished!

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.520
Go, Borreload Dragon!

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:56.490
Attack Playmaker directly!

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:02.260
Take this!  Thunder Varrel Cannon!

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:16.240
If I don’t do something this 
turn, I'll definitely lose.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.180
But what can I do?

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.360
This is…

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:33.560
The new pulse of the Cyberse inside 
my deck hasn't vanished yet.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.560
Ai, are you still there?

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.400
Can you hear me?

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.130
Answer me, Ai!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.470
Playmaker!

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.820
Whatever you try is pointless.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.440
Cyberses are already gone.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:58.820
You’re wrong.  Cyberses are still here.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.650
I can hear their pulses!

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.720
Appear, Link 4!

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.670
Firewall Dragon!

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:22.240
Fire Prison is destroyed.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:26.360
I won’t lose.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:30.280
I have three reasons why I must defeat you!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:37.360
#1: I'll defeat you and uncover the 
truth about what happened ten years ago!

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:42.960
#2: I'll regain the time that I lost!

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:47.570
#3: I'll save my friend who saved me!

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:51.320
Ten years ago…  Three things…

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:54.810
You’re the one from that 
incident ten years ago?

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:59.910
That’s right.  I'm that 
emissary of revenge!

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.280
There’s only one thing I must do.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:10.690
I'll crush the Knights of 
Hanoi and learn everything!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.180
Firewall attacks!

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.490
Tempest Attack!

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:21.170
Borreload can’t be destroyed, 
but you take damage!

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.370
It’s the removal program.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.450
Playmaker!

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.880
